{"sections":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In this tutorial you will learn about the event listeners system in Ada Engine."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"How can you catch events and process them"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"estimatedTimeInMinutes":5,"chapter":"Create your first 2D game project.","title":"Event Listeners in Ada Engine","xcodeRequirement":"Xcode 26.2 or later","kind":"hero"},{"tasks":[{"stepsSection":[],"anchor":"Base-of-Event-Subscriber-pattern","title":"Base of Event-Subscriber pattern","contentSection":[{"mediaPosition":"trailing","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Event listeners in Ada Engine are built on the Observer pattern.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Its main concept is based on the fact that there is a certain Subject that can send any events.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"And there is an Observer that can receive and process this event.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In addition, Observer “subscribes” to events, as if you had subscribed to your favorite blog or magazine - as soon as an event occurs, Observer immediately knows about it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"media":"EL-1.jpg","kind":"contentAndMedia"}]},{"stepsSection":[{"caption":[],"media":null,"code":"EL-2-1-scene.swift","runtimePreview":null,"type":"step","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Let’s say we have a plugin in which we would like to listen to some events.","type":"text"}]}]},{"caption":[],"media":null,"code":"EL-2-2-scene.swift","runtimePreview":null,"type":"step","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"First of all, to control subscription\/unsubscription to events and for proper memory management, we must create a "},{"code":"disposeBag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" using the ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Local","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property wrapper.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"We also mark our plugin with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ensure thread safety.","type":"text"}]}]},{"caption":[],"media":null,"code":"EL-2-3-scene.swift","runtimePreview":null,"type":"step","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"After that, in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"setup(in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method you can call some code to subscribe to the event.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"app.main.subscribe","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method helps with this.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"When an event is triggered, our listener subscribes to it and in the callback we can process our event.","type":"text"}]}]}],"anchor":"Subscribe-to-scene-events","title":"Subscribe to scene events","contentSection":[{"mediaPosition":"trailing","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Having understood how the Observer pattern works, let’s look at how to subscribe to scene events using the Plugin pattern."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"contentAndMedia"}]},{"stepsSection":[{"caption":[],"media":null,"code":"EL-2-3-scene.swift","runtimePreview":null,"type":"step","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In the previous section, we saw the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SceneEvents.OnReady","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" event.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"AdaEngine has several available events that you can handle.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"For example, you can find out what state your current game scene is in.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"You can add your own additional logic when any built-in event occurs.","type":"text"}]}]},{"caption":[],"media":null,"code":"EL-2-4-events.swift","runtimePreview":null,"type":"step","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Here, as an example, are some built-in events that may be useful to you.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Familiar scene events and new collision events.","type":"text"}]}]}],"anchor":"Type-of-events","title":"Type of events","contentSection":[{"mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"What events can we use? Let’s look at a couple of code examples in AdaEngine.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"stepsSection":[{"caption":[],"media":null,"code":"EL-2-5-physics.swift","runtimePreview":null,"type":"step","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Let’s continue with the example we looked at earlier.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"We can access our event and assign the necessary parameters to the properties of the physical component.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Note that we use ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task { @MainActor in ... }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ensure we’re on the main actor when modifying physics properties.","type":"text"}]}]}],"anchor":"Additional-for-physics","title":"Additional for physics","contentSection":[{"mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Additional information for handling physics in a game engine.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"With the ","type":"text"},{"code":"physicsWorld2D","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" component you can control the physics settings for any objects in our game.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"For example, you can set the gravity to zero for the scene creation event.","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"kind":"tasks"},{"action":{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/UIBasics","overridingTitle":"Get started","isActive":true,"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"Get started","type":"text"}]},"title":"UI Basics","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a simple UI screen using AdaEngine views. You will create a window, layout a few elements, and add a button with state."}],"kind":"callToAction","featuredEyebrow":"Tutorial"}],"kind":"project","hierarchy":{"modules":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/Create-your-first-2D-game-project.","projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateProject","sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateProject#Create-project-using-Xcode","kind":"task"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene","sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene#Intro","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene#Create-an-app","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene#Create-a-main-camera","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene#First-sprite","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene#Make-it-move","kind":"task"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/PlayerAndText","sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/PlayerAndText#Add-Player-component","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/PlayerAndText#Add-Text-component","kind":"task"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/EventListeners","sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/EventListeners#Base-of-Event-Subscriber-pattern","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/EventListeners#Subscribe-to-scene-events","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/EventListeners#Type-of-events","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/EventListeners#Additional-for-physics","kind":"task"}]}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/UI-and-Input","projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutori